From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: haroldxie <xiewenhao2308@icloud.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 02:48:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] mm, arm64: export execmem and set_memory_{ro,x} for the
 KJIT runtime

The KJIT runtime module installs translated user code as kernel text: it
allocates it with execmem_alloc(), writes the code and its exception
table, makes the pages read-only and executable with set_memory_rox()
(set_memory_ro() + set_memory_x() on arm64), flushes the I-cache with
flush_icache_range() (already built from exported helpers) and releases it
with execmem_free(), whose VM_FLUSH_RESET_PERMS allocation restores the
linear-map permissions. This is the life cycle of module text and of the
BPF JIT, but from a module, so these four symbols are exported GPL-only.
Nothing else changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/mm/pageattr.c | 2 ++
 mm/execmem.c             | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/mm/pageattr.c b/arch/arm64/mm/pageattr.c
index ce035e1b4..70382ea43 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/mm/pageattr.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/mm/pageattr.c
@@ -217,6 +217,7 @@ int set_memory_ro(unsigned long addr, int numpages)
 					__pgprot(PTE_RDONLY),
 					__pgprot(PTE_WRITE));
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(set_memory_ro);
 
 int set_memory_rw(unsigned long addr, int numpages)
 {
@@ -238,6 +239,7 @@ int set_memory_x(unsigned long addr, int numpages)
 					__pgprot(PTE_MAYBE_GP),
 					__pgprot(PTE_PXN));
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(set_memory_x);
 
 int set_memory_valid(unsigned long addr, int numpages, int enable)
 {
diff --git a/mm/execmem.c b/mm/execmem.c
index 084a207e4..bca0cbe27 100644
--- a/mm/execmem.c
+++ b/mm/execmem.c
@@ -478,6 +478,7 @@ void *execmem_alloc(enum execmem_type type, size_t size)
 
 	return kasan_reset_tag(p);
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(execmem_alloc);
 
 void *execmem_alloc_rw(enum execmem_type type, size_t size)
 {
@@ -505,6 +506,7 @@ void execmem_free(void *ptr)
 	if (!execmem_cache_free(ptr))
 		vfree(ptr);
 }
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(execmem_free);
 
 bool execmem_is_rox(enum execmem_type type)
 {
